<header>
	<h1>Install language packs to provide Deskpro in other languages</h1>

	<p>User interface language packs contain translations for both the user portal and for email templates. When enabled, the user can select their language from the portal.</p>


	</header>
<article>
	<section>

		<p>Agent interface language packs translate the agent interface, allowing agents who don't speak English to use Deskpro in their own language. For machine translation of either inbound messages from users or outbound responses from agents, you can enable the Microsoft Translator app, enabling agents to provide support in languages they don't speak.</p>


	<p>Once you've installed the languages you need, set the default language to be the one your helpdesk will use the most. For each language you install, you will need to enter translations for any text you have defined (like department names, custom field names, etc) using the <strong>Edit Phrases</strong> button.</p>

	</section>

	<section>
		<h2><span>FAQ</span></h2>

		<dl>
				<dt><em>Q:</em>What if I need a language that's not listed here?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
					If you have a member of staff with the right language skills, you can use our <a href="http://languages.deskpro.com/" target="_blank">crowdsourced translation system</a> to contribute new or improved translations. Alternatively, email us at <a href="mailto:support@deskpro.com">support@deskpro.com</a> to discuss other translation options.
				</dd>

			<dt><em>Q:</em>I started using the helpdesk before installing the languages I need, and now I have many tickets and users with the wrong language setting. How can I fix this?</dt>

			<dd><em>A:</em> You can change the language of tickets or users in bulk under <strong>Settings &amp; Tools</strong>.</dd>

			<dt><em>Q:</em>Users from all around the world contact my helpdesk; how do I support as many languages as possible?</dt>
			<dd><em>A:</em>
				The <strong>Settings &amp; Tools</strong> section at the lower left has an option to install and enable new language packs automatically as they become available.
			</dd>

			<dt><em>Q:</em>How do I customize the text of the user portal or agent interface?</dt>
			<dd><em>A:</em>You can add custom versions of phrases by using the <strong>Edit Phrases</strong> button.</dd>

			<dt><em>Q:</em>Why won't a variable work in my custom phrase?</dt>
			<dd><em>A:</em>See the section <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/guides/topic/401">Variables in custom phrases</a> in the Admin Manual.</dd>

			<dt><em>Q:</em>
			What's the effect of an agent setting a user's language vs a ticket's language?
			</dt>
			<dd><em>A:</em>
				The user's language is used to decide what language they see on the portal. Ticket language is for the information of agents, so that tickets can be assigned to agents with the correct language skills. By default, ticket language is set based on the user's setting, but agents can change it, for example if the user is a native French speaker but has sent a ticket in English; if there's no language set, Deskpro will try to determine the ticket language.
			</dd>

			<dt><em>Q:</em>What if I've found a translation mistake in a language pack?</dt>
				<dd><em>A:</em>
					 Please contribute your improved translation to our <a href="http://languages.deskpro.com/" target="_blank">crowdsourced translation system</a>, so it is included in future releases of Deskpro. Alternatively, if your translation change would not be applicable to other helpdesks, you can use <strong>Edit Phrases</strong> to enter a custom phrase.
				</dd>

		</dl>

	</section>

